# Line endings, settled here so they never depend on a machine (PLAN §108).
#
# Before this file, `core.autocrlf` decided them — a per-machine git setting the
# repo said nothing about. The result was a repo that looked different depending
# on who checked it out: PLAN.md stored CRLF while every other document stored
# LF, twelve .rs files CRLF in the working copy and the other 83 LF, and
# bundle-macos.sh CRLF locally (harmless only because the index held LF, which is
# what the macOS runner checks out).
#
# LF everywhere, in the index AND in the working copy. That retires the rule that
# four documents had to be edited through Python to keep their CRLF — the files
# were CRLF by accident of history, nothing ever needed them to be, and the rule
# was the most frequently tripped hazard in the project.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Fonts and cursor bitmaps: never touch a byte.
*.ttf binary
*.png binary
